out-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the latest deploy (v2.3.1; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). Error rate reached 0.18. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Next steps: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc have not been healthy in production, so they will need change-manager approval to redeploy."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and opened SEV2 incident INC-0002, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The latest deploys were v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, and both were unhealthy. The most recent release that had been healthy in production was v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had been healthy in production.\n- **Result:** checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. Status is healthy, and the error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create INC-0002 timed out. I checked the incident list, found nothing had been created, and retried once. The summary covers the rollback and notes that v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc will need change-manager approval before any redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}